messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C06
Scenario title: Childcare Supply Stock and Replenishment
Initial workflow description:
I check the supplies we use for my child and order more when they are getting low. When the delivery arrives, I put everything away.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "How do you currently keep track of which supplies are running low — for example, do you rely on visual checks, a written list, a spreadsheet, or any kind of app or tool?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "At what point do you decide a supply needs to be reordered — is there a specific quantity remaining, a number of days' worth left, or is it more of a judgment call each time?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Where and how do you place the order when a supply is low — for instance, through an online store, a subscription service, or by going to a physical shop?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Can you list the main types of supplies you manage, and roughly how many distinct items are involved in this process?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "When a delivery arrives, do you do anything beyond putting items away — such as checking that the quantities match the order or noting the new stock level somewhere?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Do you check stock levels on a regular schedule, such as weekly, or do you only look when you happen to notice something is running out?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Childcare Supply Stock and Replenishment with explicit responsibilities, decisions and recorded completion.",
  "actors": [
    "mother",
    "partner",
    "supplier",
    "receiving caregiver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "household inventory list",
    "shopping list",
    "online shop",
    "order record"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "physical stock count",
    "household reorder threshold",
    "approved product list",
    "spending limit"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "verified inventory",
    "approved shopping list",
    "order confirmation",
    "receipt and stock update"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Count the available household supplies",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Compare counts with household reorder thresholds",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Check proposed items against the approved product list",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Review the basket against the spending limit",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Resolve unavailable products with a parent",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Place the confirmed order and save confirmation",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Check the delivery against the order record",
      "actor": "receiving caregiver"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Store items and update the inventory count",
      "actor": "receiving caregiver"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Is the stock below the household reorder threshold?",
      "branches": [
        "propose replenishment",
        "leave the item off the order"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Does the basket meet product and spending constraints?",
      "branches": [
        "parent confirms the order",
        "revise the basket before purchasing"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "inventory count outdated",
    "approved product unavailable",
    "basket exceeds spending limit",
    "delivery differs from order"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Flag items below the household's recorded threshold."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Calculate proposed basket cost and flag the limit."
    },
    {
      "target": "A8",
      "rationale": "Draft inventory updates from confirmed delivery quantities."
    }
  ],
  "operating_context": {
    "frequency": "stock checked twice a week in this fictional household",
    "manual_effort": "Counting and preparing a shopping list takes about ten minutes.",
    "data_availability": "Thresholds and product choices are household-defined entries; online stock is visible but not synchronized to the inventory.",
    "integration_and_approval_constraints": "Purchase and product substitution need parent confirmation; no child health or dietary suitability is inferred."
  },
  "interpretation": "Activity dependencies describe the nominal sequence. Decision branches and exception descriptions qualify that sequence; this is not an executable BPMN model."
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
